  "notes": {
    "low_pop_tier0": "Only a handful of residential/commercial bases land in tier 0 from bbox heuristics. Candidates to promote later from exclude/ground if peon maps look too empty of hut-scale art: review exclude tall-thin rejects; do not auto-promote UI.",
    "tall_tier3": "bbox_h>=80 is tier 3 (突出した高さ). DefineSprite_633 is the 93px residential tower; keep it at 3 so pop=120 outer lots (maxTier 2) do not flood with skyscrapers.",
    "more_houses_49": "Tiny 249 retagged residential for hut-scale lots. DefineSprite_123 is the mcLoading construction timeline (115 frames), not a house cluster — keep exclude and use frontend/public/loading-build.webp.",
    "loading_build_webp": "frontend/public/loading-build.webp is built from DefineSprite_123/1–115 via scripts/build_loading_webp.py (construction rise used by mcLoading).",
    "midrise_band": "Commercial heuristic keeps tier 2 for bbox_h 52..79 so big pop still has mid-rise after tall→3. Pick is tier-first then folder-uniform so tall folder count cannot drown mid-rise.",
    "champs_farm_89": "DefineSprite_401 / 521 are Townzzy champs floor clips (auth_big_champs_gfx / auth_champs_gfx). Tag ground so farm pickers (#86) still use them while the commercial building pool does not.",
    "tree_grove_307": "DefineSprite_307 (mcHouse1 frame 7) is a tree grove clip, not a shop. Keep tag tree so Storybook and park scatter do not treat it as commercial.",
    "tree_clip_382": "DefineSprite_382 (mcHouse1 frame 15) is small tree/pine clips, not houses. Keep tag tree; no min_env so park scatter can use them (they used to spawn as tier-0 residential).",
    "exclude_promote_storybook": "Hand-promoted former exclude modules for Storybook catalog tags (226/235/242/250/257 commercial; 209/211/561/598/747 landmark; 277/281/285/294 industrial; 405 ground; 488/492/496/500/633/663 commercial). pool_eligible stays false (#82); atlas building BasesForTag still filters to building_bases.",
    "mchouse_frame_tags": "mcHouse1/2 spawn_library frames are Storybook composites of library children. frame_tags retargets mixed frames (ground/tree/residential/industrial) without changing folder-level commercial tag or map spawn pool.",
    "stamp_metadata": "stamps.* is the logical footprint + foot contract per folder (docs/map-building-placement.md). Heuristic defaults apply when omitted; stage 21 lab families are hand-tuned here."
  }
